# Store every file byte-for-byte. No line-ending translation, in either
# direction, ever.
#
# This is deliberate and it matters more here than in most repos:
#
#   - scripts/*.sh and deps/build-deps.sh are executed by `sh` INSIDE Linux
#     build containers, through a bind mount of this working tree. If git
#     ever checked them out with CRLF, every one of them would fail with
#     something unhelpful like "\r: not found". They are LF today; -text keeps
#     them that way on any machine, whatever the user's core.autocrlf says.
#
#   - third_party/libpeer/third_party/libsrtp ships CRLF from upstream. Left
#     alone, our vendored copy stays byte-identical to the commit recorded in
#     third_party/PROVENANCE.md, so `diff` against a fresh upstream checkout
#     shows real changes and not four thousand line-ending differences. That
#     property is the whole reason the provenance files exist.
#
# The cost is that git will not fix a file someone commits with the wrong
# endings. That is the right trade: silent rewriting is what breaks builds
# here, and a wrong-endings file is visible in review.
* -text

# Belt and braces for things that must never be treated as text even if the
# rule above is ever relaxed.
*.xcau   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.a      binary
*.so     binary
*.ttf    binary

# Keep GitHub's language statistics honest. Without this, third_party/ (14 MB
# of mbedTLS, libsrtp and usrsctp) swamps the ~18k lines actually written
# here, and the repository is reported as somebody else's project.
third_party/**    linguist-vendored
deps/patches/**   linguist-vendored
docs/**           linguist-documentation
